+  // spawn and keep serving; ctx->child_pid stays 0 so the SIGCHLD path that
+  // tears the session down when the leader exits simply never fires. Without
+  // this, an -X daemon has to be handed a filler program (e.g. `sleep`) purely
+  // to satisfy the exec below, and any exec failure asserts and kills X.
+  if (ctx->runprog && ctx->runprog[0]) {
